# AI Node Studio — What This Project Is

**This is OUR application.** It is a React + TypeScript web app that WE built and own. It runs locally via Vite at `http://localhost:5173`.

This is NOT ComfyUI, n8n, Glif, fal.ai, or any third-party tool. If the user shares screenshots showing nodes like "Qwen Image Edit," "Flux Pro 1.1," or "SDXL Lightning" — those are components rendered by THIS codebase. Do not ask "what platform is this" or "what tool are you using." The answer is always: this project, `ai-node-studio`.

When the user mentions models, nodes, fields, sidebars, or parameters — they are talking about code in this repo. Look at the source files below, not the internet.

## Tech Stack

React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS v4. Schema-driven dynamic UI — models declare themselves with data, the UI renders generically from schemas. No backend yet — frontend only.

## Project Structure

```
src/
  types/schema.ts          — Core types: FieldWidget, ParameterDef, PortDef, ModelSchema, NodeValues
  models/
    common-fields.ts       — Reusable parameter mixins (SEED_PARAM, OUTPUT_FORMAT_PARAM, etc.)
    registry.ts            — MODEL_REGISTRY array, getModel(), getDefaultValues()
    flux-pro.ts            — Flux Pro 1.1 schema
    qwen-image-edit.ts     — Qwen Image Edit 2511 schema
    sdxl-lightning.ts      — SDXL Lightning schema
    stable-diffusion-3.ts  — Stable Diffusion 3 schema
    real-esrgan.ts         — Real-ESRGAN x4 schema
  components/
    FieldRenderer.tsx       — Maps ParameterDef → widget component (single switch)
    Sidebar.tsx             — Renders all params for active model
    NodeCard.tsx            — Node with input/output ports
    ModelPicker.tsx         — Left panel model list
    widgets/                — SliderField, DropdownField, CheckboxField, SeedField, TextField, LoraPicker
  App.tsx                   — Layout: ModelPicker | Canvas | Sidebar
```

## How to Add a New Model

1. Create `src/models/<model-name>.ts` exporting a `ModelSchema`
2. Compose parameters from `common-fields.ts` mixins + model-specific fields
3. Import and add to `MODEL_REGISTRY` array in `src/models/registry.ts`
4. No UI code changes needed — the renderer picks it up automatically

## How to Add a New Widget Type

1. Add the new variant to the `FieldWidget` union in `src/types/schema.ts`
2. Create `src/components/widgets/<WidgetName>.tsx`
3. Add one case to the switch in `src/components/FieldRenderer.tsx`

## Key Patterns

- **Schema-driven**: Never hardcode per-model UI. Models are pure data (`ModelSchema`).
- **Composable mixins**: Common params (seed, output_format, guidance_scale) live in `common-fields.ts` and are spread into model schemas. Override defaults with `{ ...PARAM, widget: { ...overrides } }`.
- **Conditional visibility**: Parameters can declare `visibility: { dependsOn: "field_key", values: [...] }` to show/hide based on sibling field values.
- **State isolation**: Each model's values stored separately in `allValues[modelId]`.
- **Port types**: Input/output ports use `PortDef` with types: text, image, lora, number, mask, control_image.

